== four types, four questions ==
  which day    2026-08-15
  what time    14:30:00
  how long     02:30:00
  which moment 2026-08-15 14:30:00
== together and apart ==
  built       2026-08-15 14:30:00
  its day     2026-08-15
  its time    14:30:00
== how far apart ==
  the party lasted   02:30:00
  as we would say it 2h 30m
  as we would measure it, in minutes 150
  and in hours                       2.5
  the other way round -02:30:00
  its size            02:30:00
== moving around ==
  a week later  2026-08-22
  a month later 2026-09-15
  a year later  2027-08-15
  23:30 plus an hour, on a clock    00:30:00
  23:30 plus an hour, as a moment   2026-08-16 00:30:00
  and with a span                   2026-08-16 00:15:00
== which came first ==
  august before december true
  december before august false
  august is not after it true
  a day equals itself    true
  CompareTo agrees       true
  nine before nine pm    true
  a minute is shorter    true
  an hour is not shorter true
  the day is still open  true
== writing one down ==
  plain          2026-08-15 14:30:00
  just the date  2026-08-15
  just the time  14:30
  written out    August 15, 2026
  the weekday    Saturday
  how long       2h 30m
  through Format 2026-08-15
== reading one back ==
  read a date    2026-08-15
  'the fifteenth' read: false
  falling back to today's year: 2026-01-01
  25/12/2026 came back as 2026-12-25
== right now ==
  Today is midnight, having no time of day  true
  Now has one                               true
  today's date agrees with now's            true
  the clock is somewhere in the day         true
